From eed95add284069f0d93a8237dcf394b3b20f7fe7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mrm <mohammadrezam6731@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 05:36:34 +0330
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] llama: hybrid MoE cache, the CPU computes the experts
 missing from VRAM

--moe-hybrid N (with --moe-cache-mib): the experts not in the cache map
to a zero slot, a pool of N threads computes them with ggml-cpu's
vec_dot while the GPU computes the cached ones, and the result is added
after the experts. Experts are admitted by use counts that halve every
64 steps; --moe-hybrid-uploads N replaces at most N per layer step.

The slot maps, the CPU's results, the read-back of the routing and the
expert uploads use pinned memory, so their copies run in the GPU's
queue: Vulkan copies from pageable memory through a staging buffer and
waits for the GPU. The scheduler calls the copy callback before waiting
for the backend; the callbacks that need the wait synchronize.

Ornith 27B-A3B Q4_K_M on an RX 580 with a 5800 MiB cache: 94-95% of
the experts on the GPU, 32.6 tokens/s, against 28.4 for the best layer
split (-ncmoe 24) on the same build.

Also llama-bench --moe-cache-mib/--moe-hybrid/--moe-hybrid-uploads and
GGML_SCHED_TIMING=1, the host time of each graph evaluation.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
